  "transcriber_note_on_instructions": "The instruction sentence '请按照你当前的实际情况描述自己，而不是你希望自己未来能成为的样子' is transcribed as-is from the page. In the fetched text one character read '相访' where '相同' would be expected ('把和自己年龄大致相访…'), which reads like a typo on the official page or a fetch artifact — recorded here verbatim with this note rather than silently corrected.",
  "IMPORTANT_discrepancy_to_check": "The English column of this Mandarin page is NOT identical to the Johnson-120 SCORING KEY page (30FacetNEO-PI-RItems.htm). Example: this page item 28 = 'View myself as predominantly liberal politically.', but the Johnson-120 scoring key lists O6 items as 'Tend to vote for liberal political candidates.' / 'Believe that there is no absolute right and wrong.' / 'Tend to vote for conservative political candidates.' / 'Believe that we should be tough on crime.'. So this page appears to translate the ADMINISTERED questionnaire wording, which differs from the scoring-key listing. CONSEQUENCE: mapping these Chinese items to facets/dimensions requires care and should not be assumed — the parent should treat item-to-facet mapping as unverified until the full page (which may contain the mapping) is read. RESOLVED 2026-09-11 (quantified): the full page was downloaded and all 120 items parsed. The two documents are the SAME 120-item instrument, but in COMPLETELY DIFFERENT item order (position-wise identical: only 2/120; ipip-neo-120.json is grouped by facet, the Mandarin page is in administration order). By exact text identity, 117/120 Chinese items map unambiguously to a Johnson-120 scoring-key entry. The remaining 3 (zh items 28, 58, 88) are worded differently on the two pages and correspond to key entries 69, 70, 71 - all facet O6 (Openness: Values). See crosscheck_vs_ipip-neo-120 for the full numbers.",
